// expect-ok
// Z3 corpus #46: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 6 variant refinement (positive).
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// Wall 4 Step 6 admits per-variant `where` clauses on fully-named
// enum-variant payloads. The parser produces `EnumVariant.refinements`
// referencing the variant's named payload fields. The construction-site
// dispatcher at `infer_call_expr`'s enum-variant branch consults
// `universe.enum_variant_refinements` and `universe.enum_variant_field_names`
// to map the i-th positional argument (per N9-S6) to the i-th declared
// field, then runs the Step 1-style single-variable Z3 query
// `check_refinement` for the Literal-RHS path.
//
// Construction `Positive(5)` supplies the i64 payload `5`. Z3 proves
// `x > 0` (specifically `5 > 0`) — Unsat on the negation query — and
// the construction is accepted.
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
//   * Step 6 parser extension: named-payload form `V(x: i64)` (N4-S6).
//   * Step 6 parser extension: per-variant `where` clause grammar.
//   * Step 6 AST extension: `EnumVariantField { name, ty }` (cert v5).
//   * `universe.enum_variant_refinements` + `enum_variant_field_names`
//     lookup tables (N9-S6).
//   * `check_variant_refinements_at_construction` dispatcher routing.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Swapping `5` for `-1` (any value `<= 0`) flips this to T220 (fixture
// 47 demonstrates the rejecting half).
module sigil;

enum SignedInt {
    Positive(x: i64) where x > 0,
    Zero,
    Negative(x: i64) where x < 0,
}

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        let p: SignedInt = Positive(5);
        return 1;
    }
}
